  "guide": {
    "intro": [
      "Tibetan Buddhism is the form of Vajrayana and Mahayana Buddhism that took root on the Tibetan plateau. It stresses compassion, the training of the mind and a close relationship with a teacher.",
      "After 1959 many teachers left Tibet and carried the tradition around the world. Its practices use visualization, mantra, prostration and debate alongside quiet sitting."
    ],
